  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 152 AM CDT Tue Aug 25 2026\n\nWednesday night through Friday: \n\nNorthwesterly flow aloft is forecast to remain in place with\nsurface high pressure drifting across the area. This results in\nweak flow across the region. High temperatures on Thursday and \nFriday will be in the lower to mid 80s. Dewpoints on Thursday and \nFriday are forecast to be in the lower to mid 60s which should feel \ncomfortable. \n\nSaturday through Monday:\n\nBy the weekend, de-amplification of the flow pattern aloft will \noccur across the CONUS. During this change a flat ridge will be \ncentered from the southern Plains into the upper Midwest. Thus while \nmore systems will potentially be moving through the area, they will \nbe topping the ridge axis and would thus be at their weakest.\n\nAny Gulf moisture for the systems has to come up through west Texas \nbefore turning northeast into the Plains.\n\nRight now the model consensus has mainly 15-30% chances for rain \nSaturday through Monday with the better rain chances north of I-80. \nIn looking at the AIGFS and AIFS, rain chances are not as good which \nwould support a further reduction in rain chances as the week \nprogresses.",
